# backprop (Rodinia)

Back-propagation training of a layered neural network.

## Benchmark source

Rodinia Benchmark Suite 3.1 (http://lava.cs.virginia.edu/wiki/rodinia).

Contact (for the original code):

- Ke Wang: kw5na@virginia.edu
- Shuai Che: sc5nf@cs.virginia.edu
- Kevin Skadron: skadron@cs.virginia.edu

## Build

```bash
make
```

`make` builds `backprop_baseline.exe`, `backprop_pim.exe`, `backprop_pim_fast.exe`.

| Executable | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `backprop_baseline.exe` | CPU baseline |
| `backprop_pim.exe` | PUD-instrumented version; also executes every bbop on the CPU |
| `backprop_pim_fast.exe` | PUD-instrumented version without CPU execution of bbops (used by `scripts/run_workloads.sh`) |

The number of OpenMP threads is set by `NUM_THREAD` in `backprop.h`.

## Run

The only argument is the number of input units. The paper uses:

```bash
./backprop_pim_fast.exe 134217728
```

## Output

The PUD versions write `bbop_statistics.csv`, `transposition.csv`, and
`bbop_resolution.csv` to the working directory. See `../README.md` for their
format.
